WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.046 --> 00:00:10.231
After all the customers were gone, Ray handed Ally a sandwich.

2
00:00:10.232 --> 00:00:12.806
"Who's this for?" she asked.

3
00:00:12.807 --> 00:00:19.262
"You," Ray said. "You're not earning much money—the least I can do is feed you."

4
00:00:19.263 --> 00:00:27.332
"Thanks!" Ally took a bite. "Delicious!"

5
00:00:27.333 --> 00:00:32.744
Ray sighed. "Glad someone likes my food."

6
00:00:32.745 --> 00:00:38.692
Just then a boy around Ally's age walked in.

7
00:00:38.693 --> 00:00:41.854
Ally was about to hand him a menu, but the boy smiled.

8
00:00:41.855 --> 00:00:47.925
"I'm not a customer. I'm Mateo, Ray's son."

9
00:00:47.926 --> 00:00:51.517
"Hi, I'm Ally. I work here now."

10
00:00:51.518 --> 00:00:57.704
"Welcome to Ray's," Mateo said. "Hey, Papi, how was business today?"

11
00:00:57.705 --> 00:01:00.944
"Not so good," Ray replied.

12
00:01:00.945 --> 00:01:03.507
"Ally and I worked hard with just two of us.

13
00:01:03.508 --> 00:01:08.453
But that new place in town is stealing all my customers."

14
00:01:08.454 --> 00:01:17.336
"People are just going to Pepe's because it's new," Mateo said.

15
00:01:17.337 --> 00:01:24.412
"Good food should be what people care about," Ray muttered, as he went into the storeroom.

16
00:01:24.413 --> 00:01:31.700
"He's right," Mateo said. "And I bet our food is better than Pepe's."

17
00:01:31.701 --> 00:01:35.940
"The humans at Ray's are definitely better," Ally thought.

18
00:01:35.941 --> 00:01:40.066
Suddenly she spotted something familiar on Mateo's T-shirt.

19
00:01:40.067 --> 00:01:44.424
"Hey! Is that the OmegaDZed15 spaceship?"

20
00:01:44.425 --> 00:01:49.539
Mateo shrugged. "It's a model ship from the UFO museum.

21
00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:56.137
What's the OmegaDZed whatever? I'm a space geek, but I've never heard of that."

22
00:01:56.138 --> 00:01:59.454
"It's the Galorpians' star cruiser. They're a—"

23
00:01:59.455 --> 00:02:04.804
"Ally!" Ray came out of the storeroom to tell her something.

24
00:02:04.805 --> 00:02:10.034
"I'm going to close up early. I'll understand if you don't want to come back tomorrow."

25
00:02:10.035 --> 00:02:16.468
She blinked. "Did I do something wrong?"

26
00:02:16.469 --> 00:02:18.909
"Not at all," Ray said.

27
00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:23.577
"But with so few customers, you couldn't have made much money today."

28
00:02:23.578 --> 00:02:30.520
Ally had already counted her tips. "Is fifty dollars a lot?"

29
00:02:30.521 --> 00:02:40.759
"Actually, that's not bad for a slow day," Mateo said. "The customers must have liked you."

30
00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:50.761
"Come on, time to go home." Ray turned out the lights and led the way out of the diner.

31
00:02:50.762 --> 00:02:59.592
Ally left the humans and returned to her ship, which was still hidden in the park.

32
00:02:59.593 --> 00:03:07.909
Once she was back inside, she slipped off her meld medallion.

33
00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:11.356
The computer whirred to life as she sat down.

34
00:03:11.357 --> 00:03:19.874
"Scanning area, finding no new parts or fuel. Report."

35
00:03:19.875 --> 00:03:22.658
"I need to earn more money," Ally said.

36
00:03:22.659 --> 00:03:26.947
"Calculate how much I need on this planet for new parts and fuel."

37
00:03:26.948 --> 00:03:34.381
The computer clicked. "Calculating . . . $668.00."

38
00:03:34.382 --> 00:03:39.219
Ally sighed. "It's going to take longer than I expected.

39
00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:42.434
But that's okay," she added, thinking of Ray.

40
00:03:42.435 --> 00:03:46.445
"Astralians are supposed to do lots of good deeds.

41
00:03:46.446 --> 00:03:52.102
Helping Ray will give me practice for real Astralian missions."

42
00:03:52.103 --> 00:03:55.944
"Repeat warning!" The computer's lights flashed red.

43
00:03:55.945 --> 00:04:17.618
"Earthlings can be aggressive to beings from other planets! Use maximum caution!"

44
00:04:17.619 --> 00:04:24.630
When Ally arrived at the diner the next day, Ray and Mateo were eating breakfast.

45
00:04:24.631 --> 00:04:27.895
"You came back." Ray sounded surprised.

46
00:04:27.896 --> 00:04:30.875
"Of course," Ally said.

47
00:04:30.876 --> 00:04:35.506
"You sure you don't want me to stay and help today, Papi?" Mateo asked.

48
00:04:35.507 --> 00:04:45.905
Ray shook his head. "Ally's here. Go have fun at soccer camp."

49
00:04:45.906 --> 00:04:52.809
Mateo got up to leave, but he sat back down when two girls about his age walked in.

50
00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:59.826
"Two bagels to go," one said without looking up from the comm device in her hand.

51
00:04:59.827 --> 00:05:05.820
While Ally got their order ready, she noticed Mateo and the other girl smiling shyly at each other.

52
00:05:05.821 --> 00:05:10.004
"Hmm," she thought. "Interesting."

53
00:05:10.005 --> 00:05:12.854
Was there an opportunity here for another good deed?

54
00:05:12.855 --> 00:05:21.254
Ally quickly tucked her hair behind her ear.

55
00:05:21.255 --> 00:05:27.711
Then, as soon as the girls were gone, she turned to Mateo. "Do you know them?"

56
00:05:27.712 --> 00:05:36.316
"Sort of. The one with the phone is Kate, and the . . . cute one is Bethany." Mateo blushed.

57
00:05:36.317 --> 00:05:40.145
"Well, Bethany thinks you're cute too!"

58
00:05:40.146 --> 00:05:44.282
Mateo laughed. "She does not!"

59
00:05:44.283 --> 00:05:52.345
"She does!" Ally insisted. "I'm sure of it!"

60
00:05:52.346 --> 00:05:59.353
Mateo got a dreamy look on his face and seemed to float out of the diner.

61
00:05:59.354 --> 00:06:03.635
"I just made Mateo very happy!" Ally thought.

62
00:06:03.636 --> 00:06:10.132
Her parents might not think it was a big deal, but she felt very pleased.

63
00:06:10.133 --> 00:06:14.679
Just then a customer walked in.

64
00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:18.567
She wore big glasses and had a beauty mark on her cheek.

65
00:06:18.568 --> 00:06:25.831
Ally hurried over.

66
00:06:25.832 --> 00:06:29.570
"What do you recommend?" the woman asked.

67
00:06:29.571 --> 00:06:35.003
"Ray's club sandwich is the best one in the universe," Ally replied.

68
00:06:35.004 --> 00:06:38.618
"Even better than the ones on Formaria12."

69
00:06:38.619 --> 00:06:44.788
The woman looked confused. "Formaria12? Where's that restaurant?"

70
00:06:44.789 --> 00:06:50.669
"Uh . . ." Ally gulped. "Nowhere. What would you like?"

71
00:06:50.670 --> 00:06:54.582
The woman peered at Ally and then shrugged.

72
00:06:54.583 --> 00:07:01.404
"Well, if you say the sandwich is that good, then that's what I'll have."

73
00:07:01.405 --> 00:07:04.764
"Phew!" Ally thought and hurried off to the kitchen.

74
00:07:04.765 --> 00:07:09.905
That had been a close call!

